      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"about-this-notebook\">About This Notebook</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Framework Pattern Used:</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook uses <code>ts_model_framework.py</code> classes to demonstrate best practices:</span>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>ModelComparison</strong> \u2014 Orchestrates fitting + evaluation for multiple models</li>\n<li><strong>TSModel subclasses</strong> \u2014 SARIMAModel, ExponentialSmoothingModel, LightGBMModel</li>\n<li><strong>ForecastOutput</strong> \u2014 Standardised output contract (prediction, lower, upper, uncertainty_width)</li>\n<li><strong>EvaluationMetrics</strong> \u2014 Standardised metrics (mae, rmse, mape, pi_coverage, uncertainty_width)</li>\n<li><strong>TSPlotter</strong> \u2014 Generic plots that work with any model</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Why this pattern matters:</strong></span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Consistency</strong>: All models use same interface (fit \u2192 forecast)</li>\n<li><strong>Extensibility</strong>: Add new models by subclassing TSModel</li>\n<li><strong>Reusability</strong>: Plotting works for any model automatically</li>\n<li><strong>Maintainability</strong>: Changes to framework apply everywhere</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>To add a new model:</strong>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">ts_model_framework</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">TSModel</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">MyNewModel</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TSModel</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">fit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n        <span class=\"c1\"># Your fitting logic</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">pass</span>\n\n    <span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">forecast</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">steps</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">confidence_level</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">0.80</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n        <span class=\"c1\"># Your forecast logic</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">ForecastOutput</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">...</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add_model</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyNewModel</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y_train</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"c1\"># Everything else works automatically!</span>\n</code></pre></div></span></span>"
